# Task FEATURE-001-US-002-T01 — Implement: Extract calculations into testable module

> **DaemonCore coding-agent prompt.** Work type: `feature` · Size: `M` · Priority: `P1` · Status: `done`

## Where this fits
- **Epic EPIC-001 — Core Fiscal Engine.** Establish a trustworthy, deterministic and testable fiscal modelling foundation: canonical baseline data, a UI-free calculation module, static and multi-year projection calculations, validation, and regression tests.
- **Feature FEATURE-001 — Core Fiscal Engine — implementation.**
- **Story FEATURE-001-US-002 — Extract calculations into testable module.** _As a developer, I want fiscal maths separated from UI so it can be unit-tested._

## Objective
Implement the tests for: Extract calculations into testable module.

## What to do
Write **deterministic automated tests** that cover each acceptance criterion of the parent story:
- Assert: compute_fiscal() accepts baseline, revenue levers, investment levers and assumptions
- Assert: Returns static figures and a year-by-year projection structure
- Assert: model/fiscal_model.py imports no Streamlit
- Assert: app.py is reduced to control collection and rendering
Use fixed, hand-computed numbers (see `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`). Avoid randomness, network calls and time-dependence.

## Acceptance criteria (Definition of Done)
- [ ] compute_fiscal() accepts baseline, revenue levers, investment levers and assumptions
- [ ] Returns static figures and a year-by-year projection structure
- [ ] model/fiscal_model.py imports no Streamlit
- [ ] app.py is reduced to control collection and rendering
- [ ] New/updated tests pass and cover the above
- [ ] No regression in the existing `pytest` suite

## Dependencies
None within this story. (Respect cross-epic dependencies of the parent epic.)

## Project conventions
- Target Python 3.13. Use British spelling in all user-facing text.
- Keep the pure model layer (`model/`) free of Streamlit; `app.py` is UI/render only.
- Pin any new runtime deps in `requirements.txt`; test-only deps in `requirements-dev.txt`.
- Write deterministic `pytest` tests; follow the style of `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`.
- Match the surrounding code style. Prefer small, coherent diffs over broad refactors.
- Update `README.md` / `docs/` whenever behaviour changes.

## Guardrails (EPIC-001)
- All calculations live in `model/fiscal_model.py` — it must NOT import Streamlit.
- Calculations must be deterministic (no randomness).
- `baseline.csv` is the single source of truth; validate required metrics at load.
- Lock default-scenario outputs with a regression test.

## Verification
- `python3 -m py_compile model/fiscal_model.py app.py`
- `python3 -m pytest -q` — all tests pass (add/extend tests for this change).
- Boot headless once: `streamlit run app.py --server.headless true` and confirm it loads without error.

## Notes
- This simulator is a transparent scenario sandbox, not an official forecast — keep that framing in any user-facing text.
- If requirements are ambiguous or you must change a public interface, stop and flag it rather than guessing.
